nodecode-abstract is a rewrite of abstractpbc's abstractpbc/hermes-abstract-provider:

https://github.com/abstractpbc/hermes-abstract-provider
commit e322e42578586af1c376b7e836dfce437308682a
MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Abstract (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's one provider registration -- the provider id, the
base URL https://api.abstract.inc/v1, the ABSTRACT_API_KEY variable, the
output cap of 65,536 tokens, the three model ids (glm-5.3:superfast,
deepseek-v4-flash:superfast, kimi-k3:superfast) with the prices its README
publishes, and text-only input. In Nodecode that is a cell registering one
catalog row on the Responses lane, a credential hook reading the same
variable, and a round that refuses in words when no key is set.

Left out: Hermes' own ProviderProfile fields (the alias abstract-inc, the
codex_responses mode name, the auxiliary-model default and the vision flags)
that name Hermes' runtime rather than the service -- Nodecode's lane,
credential chain and model picker carry the same facts their own way. The
plugin publishes no context window and disables live model listing, so the
roster stays static here and each window is left unknown for Nodecode to
learn from the provider's own reply. No plugin code is bundled.
